# Futrob task routing

Use the matching skill; read only the workflows relevant to the request. Repository
skills are versioned with the checkout. Personal/plugin skills may not be available
in every environment; use them only when installed, with the repo contracts as authority.

| Task | Repository skill |
| --- | --- |
| Architectural decisions, ADR maintenance or task impact on architecture | [futrob-adr](../skills/futrob-adr/SKILL.md) |
| BC, use case, port, adapter or server boundary | [futrob-hexagonal-module](../skills/futrob-hexagonal-module/SKILL.md) |
| Product API consumption, SDK methods, client authentication or HTTP contracts | [futrob-sdk](../skills/futrob-sdk/SKILL.md) |
| Domain/API smoke checks or CLI commands | [futrob-cli](../skills/futrob-cli/SKILL.md) |
| Complete product screen | [create-page](../skills/create-page/SKILL.md) |
| Block within a page | [create-section](../skills/create-section/SKILL.md) |
| KPI/stat summary | [create-kpis](../skills/create-kpis/SKILL.md) |
| Contextual absence or missing prerequisites | [create-empty-state](../skills/create-empty-state/SKILL.md) |
| Stories for an existing component or composition | [add-story](../skills/add-story/SKILL.md) |
| Web styling | [futrob-stylex](../skills/futrob-stylex/SKILL.md) |
| Live verification of a user-facing web flow | [verify-futrob](../skills/verify-futrob/SKILL.md) |

The creation skills already cover stories. Use `add-story` for focused coverage work;
avoid running the same workflow twice. All design work follows [design.md](../../design.md).
The [shared composition reference](../skills/references/design-composition.md) points to
Inicio and other current pages; inspect their current source before reusing a pattern.

When available, specialist skills can support a specific need: domain/interaction
modeling, accessibility, typography, copy, colors, performance, SEO or platform APIs.
They complement the current stack and design contract; they do not select a new one.

Explicit review/operation commands remain in `.cursor/commands/`:
[ui-review](../commands/ui-review.md), [security-review](../commands/security-review.md),
[database-change](../commands/database-change.md) and [release-check](../commands/release-check.md).
Use `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` for workspace setup and standard commands.
